{"id": "EUVD-2026-88971", "enisaUuid": "6bcb624d-e172-3eac-a7f3-417ed408e32f", "description": "ClipBucket v5 through 5.5.3-#197 contains a time-based blind SQL injection vulnerability in the language update function where the language_id parameter is concatenated unescaped into the WHERE clause of an UPDATE statement. An authenticated administrator with basic_settings permission can inject arbitrary SQL payloads to extract or modify database contents.", "datePublished": "2026-09-29T14:22:38", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-06T13:36:55", "baseScore": 7.0, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:H/UI:N/VC:H/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/MacWarrior/clipbucket-v5/commit/ecbdf2d534ac7ef34a5a34e6e4c198da57d0c12c", "https://github.com/MacWarrior/clipbucket-v5/blob/f15cef1a2431786c31ffd79e81f55d6eeca4ebc0/upload/includes/classes/lang.class.php#L365", "https://hackmd.io/@leediay/two-blind-sqli-clickbucketv5-version_5_5_3_197", "https://github.com/MacWarrior/clipbucket-v5", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/clipbucket-v5-through-5.5.3-197-sql-injection-via-language-id-parameter"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-102570", "GHSA-p9pr-jwvj-678g"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.24, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "572e4318-bb89-3853-a606-39ce66b596d2", "product": {"name": "clipbucket-v5", "vendor": {"name": "MacWarrior"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22645.5.3-#197"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0e48f79c-78a8-3034-a35b-7c96dbef0e55", "vendor": {"name": "MacWarrior"}}], "isExploited": false}